    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 964,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Ethnic origins of people in Malaysia\nGiven here are the ethnic origins of Malaysian residents ( citizens , landed immigrants , and non-citizen temporary residents ) as recorded by them on their 2010 census form . The relevant census question asked for `` the ethnic or cultural origins '' of the respondent 's ancestors and not the respondents themselves . As data were collected by self-declaration , labels may not necessarily describe the true ancestry of respondents . Also note that many respondents acknowledged multiple ancestries . These people were added to the `` multiple origin '' total for each origin listed . These include responses as varied as a respondent who listed eight different origins and a respondent who answered `` Chinese Malaysian '' ( leading to him/her being counted once for `` Chinese '' and once for `` Malaysian '' ) . As with all self-reported data , understanding of the question may have varied from respondent to respondent ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
