    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 506,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "White Hispanic and Latino Americans\nIn the United States , a white Hispanic is an American citizen or resident who is racially white and of Hispanic descent . The term white , itself an official U.S. racial category , refers to people `` having origins in any of the original peoples of Europe , the Middle East , or North Africa '' . Based on the definitions created by the Office of Management and Budget and the U.S. Census Bureau , the concepts of race and ethnicity are mutually independent , and resp"
     },
     {
      "end": 1013,
      "start": 506,
      "text": "ondents to the census and other Census Bureau surveys are asked to answer both questions . Hispanicity is independent and thus not the same as race , and constitutes an ethnicity category , as opposed to a racial category , the only one of which that is officially collated by the U.S. Census Bureau . For the Census Bureau , ethnicity distinguishes between those who report ancestral origins in Spain or Hispanic America ( Hispanic and Latino Americans ) , and those who do not ( non-Hispanic Americans ) ."
     }
    ],
